# Build artefacts. `target/` alone is rooted at the context root, so it misses
# the per-agent git worktrees under .claude/, whose own target/ dirs run to
# tens of GB — enough context to exhaust the builder and fail `cargo build`
# with exit 101 and no rustc diagnostic (COX-B030's linux-build gate).
target/
**/target/
.claude/
desktop/build/
.git/
.github/
**/*.dmg
benchmark-reports/
scripts/harness/

# Never bake filled-in secrets into an image layer (COX-B030). `.env` holds the
# admin password and every backing-service credential; only the committed
# `.env.example` template belongs in the build context.
**/.env
!**/.env.example
admin-password

# CXA-B313: dependency caches and host tooling state — the image builds from
# manifests + lockfiles, never from a host-populated cache, so excluding these
# keeps the context identical to what CI builds with.
**/node_modules/
.npmrc
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/
coverage/
